- `TestRunShow_NoContentAvailable`: empty FindingsContent + missing/blank FindingsDoc → output contains "No findings content available"

Use `LocalManifestStore.NewLocalManifestStoreWithDir(dir string)` (or whatever the test helper constructor is — check manifest.go) so you don't need a real git repo for the unit tests.

### 5. Verify

```bash
go test ./cmd/entire/cli/investigate/ -count=1
mise run fmt && mise run lint
go build -o /tmp/entire-aligned ./cmd/entire
/tmp/entire-aligned investigate show --help
```

### 6. Commit

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
investigate: add `show [run-id]` subcommand

Print a saved investigation's summary + findings without needing the
per-run directory (which is auto-cleaned on Quorum/Stalled by R3).
Findings come from the manifest's embedded findings_content for
terminal outcomes, or from the on-disk findings.md for paused/
cancelled runs.

Resolution accepts a full run id, a unique prefix, or no argument when
there is exactly one manifest. Multiple-candidate cases print a
candidate list rather than guessing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)" -- cmd/entire/cli/investigate/show.go cmd/entire/cli/investigate/show_test.go cmd/entire/cli/investigate/cmd.go
```

## Report

- Status, commit SHA, files in commit
- Test results (count + pass/fail)
- Lint
- Output of `/tmp/entire-aligned investigate show --help` (paste verbatim — verify it looks right)
- Any concerns

